    "TREATMENT": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "GENERAL": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "GENERAL",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "APPROPRIATE HEALTH CARE": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "APPROPRIATE HEALTH CARE",
          "canonical_heading": "APPROPRIATE HEALTH CARE",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Following appropriate tooth-by-tooth diagnostics (periodontal probing, intraoral imaging, mobility evaluation), under anesthesia all teeth should be ultrasonically scaled, and polished; a curette should be used to remove remaining plaque and calculus accessible subgingivally.",
              "pdf_page": 661,
              "printed_page": 579,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Once the specific cause of halitosis is known, direct therapy at correcting existing pathology; often multiple teeth need to be extracted when advanced periodontal disease is the cause of halitosis.",
              "pdf_page": 661,
              "printed_page": 579,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "NURSING CARE": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "NURSING CARE",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "ACTIVITY": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "ACTIVITY",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "DIET": {
          "present": false,
          "status": "missing",
          "source_heading": null,
          "canonical_heading": "DIET",
          "content_blocks": []
        },
        "CLIENT EDUCATION": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "canonical_heading": "CLIENT EDUCATION",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Halitosis is generally a sign of an unhealthy oral cavity and should prompt oral assessment under general anesthesia, treatment, and prevention.",
              "pdf_page": 661,
              "printed_page": 579,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Initiate preventive measures to ensure good oral health (e.g., twice-daily brushing or wiping teeth, recommend accepted Veterinary Oral Heath Council products).",
              "pdf_page": 661,
              "printed_page": 579,
              "column": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Oral assessment performed under general anesthesia with intraoral radiographs and probing treatment including extraction of teeth with greater than 50% support loss.",
              "pdf_page": 661,
              "printed_page": 579,
              "column": 3
            }
          ]
        },
